{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"I can’t reliably identify the reviewed US AP agreement forms or the Irish ICAV arrangement from the context provided. In general, Rule 6c-11 permits an ETF to transact directly with an **Authorized Participant**—a registered broker-dealer or other market participant with a written agreement with the ETF—while the agreement’s main signatories are typically the **trust and the AP** (often through the adviser or distributor). The trust is a separate legal entity, commonly a registered investment company; Rule 6c-11 does not itself make it a signatory or determine its status.\n\nAn Irish ICAV is a distinct corporate fund vehicle, not a US investment-company trust. Its AP agreement may instead be entered into by the ICAV or its umbrella/sub-fund and an AP, under Irish/EU rules and its constitutional documents. The exact distinction in the reviewed forms depends on their wording, which isn’t included here."}}
